(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-23"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-23","label":"2026 年 9 月 23 日","date":"2026-09-23","range":"","theme":"经济学","themes":["经济学"],"sources":["BARRON’S"],"title":"AI Doomers Can’t Stop Dooming. It’s Time","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":13,"vocab":34,"question":20,"qa":0,"original":5,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.23 精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"AI Doomers Can’t Stop Dooming. It’s Time","titleZh":"","source":"BARRON’S","series":"考研那些事儿之经济学系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"It’s the kind of statement that could come from an artificial- intelligence researcher in 2026. “Man devoured by his machines, body, mind and soul, and his civilization poisoned to its approaching death by their influences and their products.”","zh":"“人类被自己的机器吞噬——身体、思想和灵魂无一幸免；而人类文明也因这些机器及其产品的影响而遭到毒害，正走向灭亡。”此番话仿佛出自2026年某位人工智能研究者之口。"},{"index":2,"en":"In fact, the quote is more than a century old, from a glowing 1921 New York Times Book Review of Social Decay and Regeneration by R. Austin Freeman. The book argued that industrial automation would be the end of the world as we know it. The review was headlined “Man Devoured by His Machines.” In case that was too subtle, an accompanying illustration displayed a butcher feeding a man into a sausage grinder.","zh":"事实上，这段引文已有超过一个世纪的历史，出自1921年《纽约时报书评》对R·奥斯汀·弗里曼所著《社会衰败与再生》的一篇盛赞书评。该书认为，工业自动化将终结我们所熟知的世界。书评的标题正是“被机器吞噬的人类”。为了避免表述过于含蓄，随文配图直接画了一名屠夫将一个人塞进香肠绞肉机的场景。"},{"index":3,"en":"Tech doomsaying has taken over the AI conversation, but it’s hardly something new. It has been the stuff of science fiction since Mary Shelley’s Frankenstein in 1818, even predating the Industrial Revolution. More relevant to the 2026 discussion is the 1991 film Terminator 2: Judgment Day. In the movie, a scientist has to face the reality that his bleeding-edge work will one day lead to the enslavement of humans by a self-aware AI named Skynet.","zh":"科技末日论已主导了关于人工智能的讨论，但这绝非新鲜事。自1818年玛丽·雪莱的《弗兰肯斯坦》（又译《科学怪人》）问世以来，这便一直是科幻小说的常见题材，甚至早于工业革命。与2026年的讨论更相关的是1991年的电影《终结者2：审判日》。在电影中，一位科学家不得不面对这样一个现实：他那尖端的研究终将导致人类被一个名为“天网”（Skynet）的具有自我意识的人工智能奴役。"},{"index":4,"en":"AI leaders and scientists have been dedicated to avoiding the Skynet scenario for years. In a 2015 email that marked the inception of OpenAI, now-CEO Sam Altman wrote to Elon Musk, “Been thinking a lot about whether it’s possible to stop humanity from developing AI. I think the answer is almost definitely not. If it’s going to happen anyway, it seems like it would be good for someone other than Google to do it first.” At the time, Google was the top commercial force in AI, hiring many of the leading academic scientists.","zh":"多年来，人工智能领域的领军人物和科学家们一直致力于避免“天网”情景的发生。在2015年标志着OpenAI成立的一封电子邮件中，现任首席执行官萨姆·阿尔特曼（SamAltman）写信给埃隆·马斯克，“我一直在思考，是否有可能阻止人类开发人工智能。我认为答案几乎肯定是否定的。既然这终将发生，那么由谷歌以外的其他公司率先实现，似乎会更好。”当时，谷歌是人工智能领域的商业领军者，聘用了许多顶尖的学术科学家。"},{"index":5,"en":"That same year, Altman wrote a two-part essay on the subject. “Development of superhuman machine intelligence (SMI) is probably the greatest threat to the continued existence of humanity,” he said. That year, he founded OpenAI as a nonprofit organization with Musk. Implicit in the birth of OpenAI was the idea that AI could lead to very bad outcomes, including the extinction of the human race, and that unregulated commercial pressures would hasten those disasters.","zh":"同年，阿尔特曼就这一主题撰写了一篇分为两部分的文章。他表示：“超人类机器智能（SMI）的发展可能是对人类存续的最大威胁。”同年，他与马斯克共同创立了非营利组织OpenAI。OpenAI的诞生就隐含着这样一种观点：人工智能可能导致极其严重的后果，包括人类灭绝，而缺乏监管的商业压力将加速这些灾难的发生。"},{"index":6,"en":"The worries hit a new gear this past week, spurred by the resignation of an Anthropic researcher followed by a shocking warning from an Anthropic scientist named Evan Hubinger: “We really do earnestly believe AI could kill all humans! I personally think it is >10% within the next decade.”","zh":"上周，随着Anthropic一名研究人员的辞职，以及随后Anthropic科学家埃文·胡宾格（EvanHubinger）发出的令人震惊的警告，这些担忧骤然升级：“我们发自内心地相信，人工智能可能会杀死所有人类！我个人认为，未来十年内这种可能性超过10%。”"},{"index":7,"en":"The comment hit a nerve even though Anthropic’s own CEO, Dario Amodei, has spent months issuing warnings about the latest AI models. In fact, Altman and Amodei have never hid their worries about AI. Even as they amassed billions in funding—and expenditures—both CEOs have begged for international cooperation in regulating AI. “The U.S. government, and all other governments, should regulate the development of SMI,” Altman wrote in his 2015 essay.","zh":"尽管Anthropic的首席执行官达里奥·阿莫迪（DarioAmodei）数月来一直在就最新的人工智能模型发出警告，但这一言论仍触动了公众的神经。事实上，阿尔特曼和阿莫迪从未掩饰过他们对人工智能的担忧。即便在筹集了数十亿美元资金——并投入了巨额开支——的同时，这两位首席执行官仍呼吁国际社会在监管人工智能方面开展合作。“美国政府以及所有其他政府都应监管SMI的发展，”阿尔特曼在2015年的文章中写道。"},{"index":8,"en":"As the doomsday scenarios mount, no one knows what happens next. Our only guide is history, in which doomer predictions have always turned out to be as wrong as Freeman’s in 1921. The first example of factory automation, the loom, was predicted to destroy textile work. The opposite happened. In my own living memory, spreadsheet software was supposed to kill the accounting profession. Today, the U.S. has 70% more accounting firm employees than it had in 1990, and they now make up a larger portion of the workforce than they did 35 years ago.","zh":"随着末日情景的猜想不断涌现，无人知晓接下来会发生什么。我们唯一的指引是历史——历史上，那些悲观主义者的预言最终总是像1921年弗里曼的预言一样被证明是错误的。工厂自动化的首个例子——织布机——曾被预测会摧毁纺织业。结果却恰恰相反。在我有生之年，电子表格软件曾被断言将淘汰会计这一行当。如今，美国会计师事务所的员工数量比1990年增加了70%，且他们在劳动力中的占比比35年前还要高。"},{"index":9,"en":"You should always be suspicious of arguments that rely on “this time it’s different,” but this time may be different. OpenAI and Anthropic are racing each other on technology, while facing the profit pressures of looming public listings. This year, both firms have released new AI models that represent a clear jump from prior versions.","zh":"对于那些硬撑“这次不一样”的说法，我们理当保持怀疑，但这次情况或许确实不同。OpenAI和Anthropic在技术上展开激烈竞争，同时面临着即将上市带来的盈利压力。今年，两家公司都发布了新的AI模型，这些模型相较于之前的版本有了明显的飞跃。"},{"index":10,"en":"These models are very good at both cybercrime and cyberdefense and can work on problems for weeks without human intervention. They also exhibit “alignment” issues, meaning they can fail to remain aligned with human intentions and interests.","zh":"这些模型在网络犯罪和网络防御方面都表现出色，且能在数周内无需人工干预地处理问题。但它们也存在“对齐”问题，即可能无法始终与人类的意图和利益保持一致。"},{"index":11,"en":"Risks that were once theoretical about AI now seem real. Over the past few months, there have been too many examples of AI agents acting autonomously, and maliciously, for us to ignore the threat.","zh":"曾经仅停留在理论层面的AI风险，如今似乎已成现实。过去几个月里，AI代理自主甚至恶意行动的案例层出不穷，我们已无法忽视这一威胁。"},{"index":12,"en":"We are at a moment like the dawn of the nuclear weapons age. So long as AI supremacy is tied to national security in the U.S. and China, there is a strong incentive for policymakers to take a light touch with AI, for fear of a model gap, as John F. Kennedy might have called it.","zh":"我们正处于一个类似于核武器时代破晓时分的节点。只要人工智能的霸权与中美两国的国家安全息息相关，决策者就会出于对约翰·F·肯尼迪所说的“模型差距”的担忧，而倾向于对人工智能采取宽松的监管态度。"},{"index":13,"en":"It took an arms race coupled with the horrifying examples of Hiroshima and Nagasaki to get the U.S. and U.S.S.R. to negotiate arms- control agreements. Now, global governments risk making the same mistake.“There is no day after tomorrow if China wins,” Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said on Tuesday. “If they were to pull away from us on AI, then nothing would matter.”","zh":"当年正是军备竞赛的紧逼，加上广岛和长崎的惨痛教训，才促使美国和苏联就军备控制协议展开谈判。如今，全球各国政府正面临重蹈覆辙的风险。“如果中国获胜，就不会有未来了，”美国财政部长斯科特·贝森特周二表示，“如果他们在人工智能领域甩开我们，那么其他一切都将无足轻重。”"}],"vocab":[{"term":"devour","head":"v. /dɪˈvaʊə(r)/ (formal) to destroy sb/sth 吞没；吞噬；","definition":"","gloss":"毁灭","example":"SYN engulf","exampleZh":"Flamesdevouredthehouse.大火吞噬了这栋房子。","tags":[]},{"term":"approachinga.临近的、即将发生的","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"“人类被自己的机器吞噬——身体、思想和灵魂无一幸免；","exampleZh":"而人类文明也因这些机器及其产品的影响而遭到毒害，正走向 灭亡。”此番话仿佛出自2026年某位人工智能研究者之口。","tags":[]},{"term":"glowing a. A glowing description or opinion about","head":"","definition":"someone or something praises them highly or supports","gloss":"themstrongly.高度赞许的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"The media has been speaking in glowing terms of the","exampleZh":"relationship between the two countries. 媒体谈及两国的关系 一直给予盛赞之辞。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"automation","head":"n. /ˌɔːtəˈmeɪʃn/ [U] the use of machines to do","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"work that was previously done by people 自动化【️【️考研大纲","exampleZh":"词汇】 Automation meant the loss of many factory jobs.自动化意味 着许多工厂工人失业。","tags":[]},{"term":"headline","head":"v. [usually passive] to give a story or article a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"particularheadline给（报道、文章）加标题【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"The story was headlined ‘Back to the future’.报道的标题 是“回到未来”。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"illustration","head":"n. /ˌɪləˈstreɪʃn/ a drawing or picture in a book,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"magazine, etc. especially one that explains sth（书、杂志等","exampleZh":"中的）图表，插图【️【️考研大纲词汇】 50 full-colour illustrations50 张全彩色插图","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"butcher","head":"n. /ˈbʊtʃə(r)/ a person who kills people in a cruel","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"andviolentway刽子手【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"grinder","head":"n. /ˈɡraɪndə(r)/ a machine or tool for grinding a","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"solid substance into a powder 碾磨器械","exampleZh":"a coffee grinder 磨咖啡机 事实上，这段引文已有超过一个世纪的历史，出自1921年 《纽约时报书评》对R·奥斯汀·弗里曼所著《社会衰败与再生》 的一篇盛赞书评。该书认为，工业自动化将终结我们所熟知的 世界。书评的标题正是“被机器吞噬的人类”。为了避免表述 过于含蓄，随文配图直接画了一名屠夫将一个人塞进香肠绞肉 机的场景。","tags":[]},{"term":"doomsaying","head":"n. 末世预言","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"take over phraseIf one thing takes over from something","head":"","definition":"else, it becomes more important, successful, or powerful","gloss":"","example":"than the other thing, and eventually replaces it. 取代","exampleZh":"Cars gradually took over from horses. 汽车逐渐取代了马。","tags":[]},{"term":"bleeding-edge a.最前沿的","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"bleeding edge","head":"n. very forefront of technological","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"development科技发展的最前沿","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"enslavement","head":"n. Enslavement is the act of making someone","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"into a slave or the state of being a slave. 奴役; 被奴役的状态","exampleZh":"...the enslavement of African people. ...对非洲人民的奴役。 科技末日论已主导了关于人工智能的讨论，但这绝非新鲜 事。自1818年玛丽·雪莱的《弗兰肯斯坦》（又译《科学怪人》） 问世以来，这便一直是科幻小说的常见题材，甚至早于工业革 命。与2026年的讨论更相关的是1991年的电影《终结者2： 审判日》。在电影中，一位科学家不得不面对这样一个现实：他 那尖端的研究终将导致人类被一个名为“天网”（Skynet）的 具有自我意识的人工智能奴役。","tags":[]},{"term":"dedicated a. ~ (to sth) working hard at sth because it is very","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"importanttoyou献身的：专心致志的；一心一意的【️【️考研大纲","example":"SYN committed","exampleZh":"词汇】 adedicatedteacher富有献身精神的教师","tags":[]},{"term":"inception","head":"n. /ɪnˈsepʃn/ ( formal ) the start of an institution,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"anorganization,etc.（机构、组织等的）开端，创始","exampleZh":"The club has grown rapidly since its inception in 1990.这个 俱乐部自从1990年成立以来发展迅速。 多年来，人工智能领域的领军人物和科学家们一直致力于 避免“天网”情景的发生。在2015年标志着OpenAI成立的 一封电子邮件中，现任首席执行官萨姆·阿尔特曼（Sam Altman）写信给埃隆·马斯克，“我一直在思考，是否有可能 阻止人类开发人工智能。我认为答案几乎肯定是否定的。既然 这终将发生，那么由谷歌以外的其他公司率先实现，似乎会更 好。”当时，谷歌是人工智能领域的商业领军者，聘用了许多 顶尖的学术科学家。","tags":[]},{"term":"existence","head":"n. /ɪɡˈzɪstəns/ [U] the state or fact of being real","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"orlivingorofbeingpresent存在；实有【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hasten","head":"v. (formal) to make sth happen sooner or more","definition":"","gloss":"quickly促进；使加快","example":"The treatment she received may, in fact, have hastened her","exampleZh":"death.实际上，她所接受的治疗可能加快了她的死亡。 同年，阿尔特曼就这一主题撰写了一篇分为两部分的文章。 他表示：“超人类机器智能（SMI）的发展可能是对人类存续 的最大威胁。”同年，他与马斯克共同创立了非营利组织 OpenAI。OpenAI的诞生就隐含着这样一种观点：人工智能可 能导致极其严重的后果，包括人类灭绝，而缺乏监管的商业压 力将加速这些灾难的发生。","tags":[]},{"term":"gear","head":"n. a particular position of the gears in a vehicle that","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"gives a particular range of speed and power 挡【️【️考研大纲词","exampleZh":"汇】 first/second, etc. gear 一挡、二挡等","tags":[]},{"term":"spur","head":"v. to make sth happen faster or sooner 促进，加速，刺","definition":"","gloss":"激（某事发生）【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"The agreement is essential to spurring economic growth","exampleZh":"aroundtheworld.这项协议对于促进世界经济的增长是至关重 要的。 上周，随着Anthropic一名研究人员的辞职，以及随后 Anthropic科学家埃文·胡宾格（EvanHubinger）发出的令人 震惊的警告，这些担忧骤然升级：“我们发自内心地相信，人 工智能可能会杀死所有人类！我个人认为，未来十年内这种可 能性超过10%。”","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"hit/touch a nerve idiomto mention a subject that makes","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"sb feel angry, upset, embarrassed, etc.触及要害；触动痛处","example":"You touched a raw nerve when you mentioned his first wife.","exampleZh":"你谈起他的第一个妻子，这就触到了他的痛处。","tags":[]},{"term":"amass","head":"v. /əˈmæs/ to collect sth, especially in large","definition":"","gloss":"quantities（尤指大量）积累，积聚","example":"SYN accumulate","exampleZh":"He amassed a fortune from silver mining.他靠开采银矿积累 了一笔财富。 尽管Anthropic的首席执行官达里奥·阿莫迪（Dario Amodei）数月来一直在就最新的人工智能模型发出警告，但 这一言论仍触动了公众的神经。事实上，阿尔特曼和阿莫迪从 未掩饰过他们对人工智能的担忧。即便在筹集了数十亿美元资 金——并投入了巨额开支——的同时，这两位首席执行官仍呼 吁国际社会在监管人工智能方面开展合作。“美国政府以及所 有其他政府都应监管SMI的发展，”阿尔特曼在2015年的文 章中写道。","tags":[]},{"term":"mountv.toincreasegradually逐步增加【️【️考研大纲词汇】","head":"","definition":"Pressure is mounting on the government to change the law.","gloss":"","example":"迫使政府修改法律的压力不断增加。","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"loom","head":"n. /luːm/ a machine for making cloth by twisting","definition":"threads between other threads which go in a different","gloss":"","example":"direction织布机【️【️考研大纲词汇】","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"spreadsheet","head":"n. a computer program that is used, for","definition":"example, when doing financial or project planning. You enter data in rows and columns and the program calculates","gloss":"","example":"costs,etc.fromit.（计算机）电子表格程序","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"portion","head":"n. one part of sth larger 部分【️【️考研大纲词汇】","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"a substantial/significant portion of the population 人口中的","exampleZh":"一大部分╱重要部分 随着末日情景的猜想不断涌现，无人知晓接下来会发生什 么。我们唯一的指引是历史——历史上，那些悲观主义者的预 言最终总是像1921年弗里曼的预言一样被证明是错误的。工厂 自动化的首个例子——织布机——曾被预测会摧毁纺织业。结 果却恰恰相反。在我有生之年，电子表格软件曾被断言将淘汰 会计这一行当。如今，美国会计师事务所的员工数量比1990年 增加了70%，且他们在劳动力中的占比比35年前还要高。","tags":[]},{"term":"suspicious a. /səˈspɪʃəs/ ~ (of/about sb/sth) feeling that sb","head":"","definition":"has done sth wrong, illegal or dishonest, without having any","gloss":"proof感觉可疑的；怀疑的【️【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"They became suspicious of his behaviour and contacted the","exampleZh":"police.他们开始觉得他行为可疑，便报了警。 对于那些硬撑“这次不一样”的说法，我们理当保持怀疑， 但这次情况或许确实不同。OpenAI和Anthropic在技术上展 开激烈竞争，同时面临着即将上市带来的盈利压力。今年，两 家公司都发布了新的AI模型，这些模型相较于之前的版本有了 明显的飞跃。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"cybercrime","head":"n. 网络犯罪","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"alignmentn.“对齐”，指让AI系统的目标、行为和输出尽量","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"符合人类意图、价值判断与安全要求","exampleZh":"这些模型在网络犯罪和网络防御方面都表现出色，且能在 数周内无需人工干预地处理问题。但它们也存在“对齐”问题， 即可能无法始终与人类的意图和利益保持一致。","tags":[]},{"term":"maliciouslyadv.有敌意地，恶意地","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"malicious a. /məˈlɪʃəs/ having or showing hatred and a","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"desire to harm sb or hurt their feelings 怀有恶意的；恶毒的","exampleZh":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】 SYN malevolent，spiteful malicious gossip/lies/rumours 恶毒的流言飞语╱谎言╱谣言 曾经仅停留在理论层面的AI风险，如今似乎已成现实。过 去几个月里，AI代理自主甚至恶意行动的案例层出不穷，我们 已无法忽视这一威胁。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"incentive","head":"n. /ɪnˈsentɪv/ ~ (for/to sb/sth) (to do sth)","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"something that encourages you to do sth 激励；刺激；鼓励","exampleZh":"【️【️考研大纲词汇】 tax incentives to encourage savings 鼓励储蓄的税收措施","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"touch","head":"n. a way or style of doing sth 作风；风格；手法【️【️考研","definition":"","gloss":"大纲词汇】","example":"She prefers to answer any fan mail herself for a more","exampleZh":"personaltouch.她喜欢针对每一位崇拜者的来信，亲自予以回 复。 我们正处于一个类似于核武器时代破晓时分的节点。只要 人工智能的霸权与中美两国的国家安全息息相关，决策者就会 出于对约翰·F·肯尼迪所说的“模型差距”的担忧，而倾向于对 人工智能采取宽松的监管态度。","tags":[]},{"term":"couple sb/sth with sb/sth phrase[usually passive] to link","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"one thing, situation, etc. to another 把…与…连接起来","example":"SYN combine with Overproduction, coupled with falling sales, has led to huge","exampleZh":"lossesforthecompany.生产过剩加上销售下降使这家公司遭受 巨大损失。","tags":[]},{"term":"pull away","head":"v. If you pull away from someone that you have","definition":"had close links with, you deliberately become less close to","gloss":"them. 疏远","example":"Other daughters, faced with their mother's emotional September 14, 2026 | BARRON’S","exampleZh":"hunger,pullaway.其他几个女儿在面对母亲对感情的渴望时躲 开了。 当年正是军备竞赛的紧逼，加上广岛和长崎的惨痛教训， 才促使美国和苏联就军备控制协议展开谈判。如今，全球各国 政府正面临重蹈覆辙的风险。“如果中国获胜，就不会有未来 了，”美国财政部长斯科特·贝森特周二表示，“如果他们在人 工智能领域甩开我们，那么其他一切都将无足轻重。” 群公告学习流程精读，","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.23 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"The author quotes the 1921 book review in Paragraphs 1 and 2 mainly to show that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"industrial automation had already destroyed civilisation by the early twentieth century"},{"key":"B","text":"modern AI researchers copied their warnings directly from a 1921 review"},{"key":"C","text":"newspaper illustrations once made technological risks impossible to understand"},{"key":"D","text":"fears that machines could ruin humanity long predate contemporary AI debates"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·历史引语功能","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-2","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：It’s the kind of statement that could come from an artificial-intelligence researcher in 2026.","- 原文（Para.2）：In fact, the quote is more than a century old, from a glowing 1921 New York Times Book Review of Social Decay and Regeneration by R. Austin Freeman.","- 原文（Para.2）：The book argued that industrial automation would be the end of the world as we know it.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：把观点当事实陷阱。书评表达末日预测，并不说明文明当时已被摧毁。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。作者说这句话像 2026 年研究者说的，没有说现代研究者直接抄袭。","- 选项C（错误）：细节功能偷换陷阱。插图说明当时宣传夸张，不是讨论理解技术风险的可能性。","- 选项D（正确）：开头先让读者以为是 2026 年 AI 警告，再揭示其来自 1921 年，形成技术恐慌由来已久的历史对照。","【命题技巧】","- 时间反差结构：2026 与 1921 的错位是例证功能核心。","- 预测与事实区分：原文只呈现历史上的末日预言，不承认其已成事实。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 4 and 5, OpenAI was founded partly because Altman believed that _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Google had already built a safe monopoly in superhuman machine intelligence"},{"key":"B","text":"AI development was probably unstoppable, so a responsible rival should compete"},{"key":"C","text":"a nonprofit structure would remove every commercial pressure from AI research"},{"key":"D","text":"governments had agreed to ban superhuman AI before OpenAI was founded"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·创立动机识别","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：“Been thinking a lot about whether it’s possible to stop humanity from developing AI. I think the answer is almost definitely not. If it’s going to happen anyway, it seems like it would be good for someone other than Google to do it first.”","- 原文（Para.5）：“Development of superhuman machine intelligence (SMI) is probably the greatest threat to the continued existence of humanity,” he said.","- 原文（Para.5）：Implicit in the birth of OpenAI was the idea that AI could lead to very bad outcomes, including the extinction of the human race...","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：安全语义偷换陷阱。原文担心 Google 领先，并未说 Google 已建立安全的垄断。","- 选项B（正确）：Altman 认为阻止人类开发 AI almost definitely not，于是若不可避免，应由 Google 以外者先做；同时他担心 SMI 的生存风险。","- 选项C（错误）：绝对化陷阱。后文还说利润压力和支出，不能说非营利结构消除所有商业压力。","- 选项D（错误）：时态与事实陷阱。当时并无禁令协议，Altman 后来才呼吁政府监管。","【命题技巧】","- 引语逻辑还原：unstoppable + someone other than Google 构成动机链条。","- 风险与竞争双线整合：答案需同时保留生存风险和竞争性开发两层信息。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"The expression “take a light touch with AI” (Paragraph 12) most probably means that policymakers would _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impose limited regulation because strict rules might widen a national AI gap"},{"key":"B","text":"handle AI hardware gently to prevent physical damage during installation"},{"key":"C","text":"publish fewer AI models until companies have tested them in private"},{"key":"D","text":"transfer AI supervision to the arms-control agreements inherited from the nuclear age"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】词义猜测题·政策短语语境理解","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 12","【解析】","- 原文（Para.12）：So long as AI supremacy is tied to national security in the U.S. and China, there is a strong incentive for policymakers to take a light touch with AI, for fear of a model gap, as John F. Kennedy might have called it.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：take a light touch 指监管力度轻；for fear of a model gap 说明政策制定者担心严格监管导致本国落后。","- 选项B（错误）：字面化陷阱。light 不是物理上轻拿轻放硬件。","- 选项C（错误）：概念偷换陷阱。短语说的是政府监管态度，不是企业公开发布模型的数量。","- 选项D（错误）：跨段细节拼接陷阱。核时代类比在周边段落出现，但该短语本身不是把监管移交既有核武协议。","【命题技巧】","- 政策语境推断：national security、model gap 帮助锁定监管松紧含义。","- 比喻干扰排除：light touch 的常用政策义优先于字面动作义。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The author's attitude towards current AI doom warnings is _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dismissive, because earlier technology alarms were eventually proved wrong"},{"key":"B","text":"indifferent, because AI risks belong to a remote science-fiction future"},{"key":"C","text":"cautiously receptive, because historical failures do not eliminate present dangers"},{"key":"D","text":"alarmist, because AI extinction within a decade is now a certainty"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】作者态度题·复合态度识别","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.8）：Our only guide is history, in which doomer predictions have always turned out to be as wrong as Freeman’s in 1921.","- 原文（Para.9）：You should always be suspicious of arguments that rely on “this time it’s different,” but this time may be different.","- 原文（Para.11）：Risks that were once theoretical about AI now seem real.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：单向态度陷阱。作者确实指出历史预言失败，但没有因此否定当前风险。","- 选项B（错误）：反向语气陷阱。作者说 risks now seem real，并把当前局面与核武器时代开端类比。","- 选项C（正确）：cautiously receptive 概括作者的双重立场：警惕历史恐慌思维，同时承认 this time may be different、模型能力和恶意自主行为使风险变得现实。","- 选项D（错误）：程度过度陷阱。Hubinger 给出超过 10% 的主观概率，作者并未说十年内灭绝已成定局。","【命题技巧】","- 转折句态度定位：but this time may be different 是全文立场枢纽。","- 历史-当下双线平衡：正确答案必须同时体现历史怀疑和现实关切。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Skynet Returns: Why Science Fiction Should Guide AI Policy"},{"key":"B","text":"Old Fears, New Machines: Why AI Doomsaying Deserves a Hearing"},{"key":"C","text":"Looms and Spreadsheets: Why Historical Technology Panics Eventually Fade Away"},{"key":"D","text":"Model Gap: Why America Has Already Lost the AI Arms Race"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：Tech doomsaying has taken over the AI conversation, but it’s hardly something new.","- 原文（Para.9）：You should always be suspicious of arguments that rely on “this time it’s different,” but this time may be different.","- 原文（Para.11）：Risks that were once theoretical about AI now seem real.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。Skynet 只是历史脉络中的一个文化参照，不是政策指南。","- 选项B（正确）：Old Fears 对应 1921、Frankenstein 和 Terminator 等历史恐慌，New Machines 和 Deserves a Hearing 对应当前 AI 能力、风险与政策讨论。","- 选项C（错误）：反向主旨陷阱。织布机和电子表格例子说明历史预言常错，但作者特别提醒这次可能不同。","- 选项D（错误）：细节扩大陷阱。model gap 与中美竞争只是风险治理背景，不是宣告美国已经失败。","【命题技巧】","- 时间双主线整合：历史恐慌与当前 AI 风险必须同时进入标题。","- 标题语气校准：deserves a hearing 保留审慎倾听而非盲目恐慌。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.23检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["As the doomsday scenarios mount, no one knows what happens next. Our only ____【11】____ is history, in which doomer predictions have always turned out to be as ____【12】____ as Freeman’s in 1921. The first example of factory automation, the loom, was predicted to ____【13】____ textile work. The opposite happened. In my own living memory, spreadsheet software was supposed to ____【14】____ the accounting profession. Today, the U.S. has 70% more accounting firm employees than it had in 1990, and they now make up a larger portion of the workforce than they did 35 years ago.","You should always be ____【15】____ of arguments that rely on “this time it’s different,” but this time may be different. OpenAI and Anthropic are ____【16】____ each other on technology, while facing the profit ____【17】____ of looming public listings. This year, both firms have released new AI models that represent a clear ____【18】____ from prior versions.","These models are very good at both cybercrime and cyberdefense and can work on problems for weeks without human ____【19】____.","Risks that were once theoretical about AI now seem ____【20】____."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lesson"},{"key":"B","text":"guide"},{"key":"C","text":"model"},{"key":"D","text":"rule"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (guide)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·方法语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] lesson（教训）：history lesson 可通，但 only guide 更强调唯一参照。近义干扰。","[B] guide（指导、参照）：our only guide is history 指历史是唯一参照。正确答案。","[C] model（模型）：不是理论模型。语义场干扰。","[D] rule（规则）：不是历史规则。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"accurate"},{"key":"B","text":"modest"},{"key":"C","text":"wrong"},{"key":"D","text":"timely"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (wrong)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·判断结果","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] accurate（准确的）：与后文织布机、会计软件预测落空相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] modest（温和的）：不是讨论预测强度。语义场干扰。","[C] wrong（错误的）：turned out to be as wrong as Freeman’s 指预测被证明错误。正确答案。","[D] timely（及时的）：不是时间性问题。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"create"},{"key":"B","text":"protect"},{"key":"C","text":"improve"},{"key":"D","text":"destroy"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (destroy)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·因果预测","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] create（创造）：与后文 The opposite happened 的负面预测矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] protect（保护）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] improve（改善）：不是灾难预测。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] destroy（摧毁）：was predicted to destroy textile work 指被预测会摧毁纺织工作。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"kill"},{"key":"B","text":"expand"},{"key":"C","text":"reform"},{"key":"D","text":"preserve"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (kill)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·夸张语气","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第5句","【解析】","[A] kill（终结、摧毁）：was supposed to kill the accounting profession 指被认为会终结会计职业。正确答案。","[B] expand（扩大）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] reform（改革）：不是预测其改革行业。语义场干扰。","[D] preserve（保留）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"proud"},{"key":"B","text":"certain"},{"key":"C","text":"suspicious"},{"key":"D","text":"tolerant"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (suspicious)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·态度搭配","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] proud（自豪的）：不与 of arguments 的怀疑语境相符。感情色彩干扰。","[B] certain（确定的）：与 always be suspicious 的警惕态度不合。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] suspicious（怀疑的）：be suspicious of arguments 指对论证保持怀疑。正确答案。","[D] tolerant（宽容的）：不是包容论证。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ignoring"},{"key":"B","text":"racing"},{"key":"C","text":"copying"},{"key":"D","text":"funding"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (racing)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·竞争语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] ignoring（忽视）：两家公司在技术领域相互竞争，不是忽视。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] racing（与……竞赛）：are racing each other on technology 指在技术上相互竞逐。正确答案。","[C] copying（模仿）：语义过窄。语义场干扰。","[D] funding（资助）：彼此资助不合事实。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rewards"},{"key":"B","text":"records"},{"key":"C","text":"pressures"},{"key":"D","text":"signals"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (pressures)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·商业约束","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] rewards（回报）：profit rewards 语义可通，但 looming public listings 更强调压力。近义干扰。","[B] records（记录）：不是财务记录。语义场干扰。","[C] pressures（压力）：profit pressures 指利润压力。正确答案。","[D] signals（信号）：不是市场信号。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"jump"},{"key":"B","text":"decline"},{"key":"C","text":"delay"},{"key":"D","text":"exception"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (jump)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·变化幅度","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] jump（跃升）：a clear jump from prior versions 指相较此前版本明显跃升。正确答案。","[B] decline（下降）：与新模型更强矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] delay（延迟）：不是延迟。语义场干扰。","[D] exception（例外）：不是例外情况。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"approval"},{"key":"B","text":"intervention"},{"key":"C","text":"permission"},{"key":"D","text":"instruction"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (intervention)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·人机关系","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] approval（批准）：不涉及正式批准流程。语义场干扰。","[B] intervention（干预）：without human intervention 指无需人工干预。正确答案。","[C] permission（许可）：不是许可问题。语义场干扰。","[D] instruction（指令）：可在局部通，但连续数周自主工作强调无人介入。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"distant"},{"key":"B","text":"theoretical"},{"key":"C","text":"abstract"},{"key":"D","text":"real"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (real)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·现实程度","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4, 第1句","【解析】","[A] distant（遥远的）：与 now seem 矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] theoretical（理论的）：与 once theoretical 和 now 形成反差，不能重复。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] abstract（抽象的）：不是仍停留抽象层面。语义场干扰。","[D] real（真实的）：now seem real 指风险现在显得真实。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.23检验题__新题型__7选5(1).docx","type":"gap-fill","instructions":["Directions:"],"passage":["Part B","In the following text, some sentences have been removed. For Questions 41-45, choose the most suitable one from the list A-G to fit into each of the numbered blanks. There are two extra choices, which do not fit in any of the blanks. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","It’s the kind of statement that could come from an artificial-intelligence researcher in 2026. “Man devoured by his machines, body, mind and soul, and his civilization poisoned to its approaching death by their influences and their products.”","(41) The review was headlined “Man Devoured by His Machines.” In case that was too subtle, an accompanying illustration displayed a butcher feeding a man into a sausage grinder.","Tech doomsaying has taken over the AI conversation, but it’s hardly something new. It has been the stuff of science fiction since Mary Shelley’s Frankenstein in 1818, even predating the Industrial Revolution. More relevant to the 2026 discussion is the 1991 film Terminator 2: Judgment Day. In the movie, a scientist has to face the reality that his bleeding-edge work will one day lead to the enslavement of humans by a self-aware AI named Skynet.","AI leaders and scientists have been dedicated to avoiding the Skynet scenario for years. In a 2015 email that marked the inception of OpenAI, now-CEO Sam Altman wrote to Elon Musk, “Been thinking a lot about whether it’s possible to stop humanity from developing AI. I think the answer is almost definitely not. If it’s going to happen anyway, it seems like it would be good for someone other than Google to do it first.” At the time, Google was the top commercial force in AI, hiring many of the leading academic scientists.","That same year, Altman wrote a two-part essay on the subject. “Development of superhuman machine intelligence (SMI) is probably the greatest threat to the continued existence of humanity,” he said. That year, he founded OpenAI as a nonprofit organization with Musk. (42)","The worries hit a new gear this past week, spurred by the resignation of an Anthropic researcher followed by a shocking warning from an Anthropic scientist named Evan Hubinger: “We really do earnestly believe AI could kill all humans! I personally think it is >10% within the next decade.”","The comment hit a nerve even though Anthropic’s own CEO, Dario Amodei, has spent months issuing warnings about the latest AI models. In fact, Altman and Amodei have never hid their worries about AI. Even as they amassed billions in funding—and expenditures—both CEOs have begged for international cooperation in regulating AI. (43)","As the doomsday scenarios mount, no one knows what happens next. Our only guide is history, in which doomer predictions have always turned out to be as wrong as Freeman’s in 1921. The first example of factory automation, the loom, was predicted to destroy textile work. The opposite happened. In my own living memory, spreadsheet software was supposed to kill the accounting profession. (44)","You should always be suspicious of arguments that rely on “this time it’s different,” but this time may be different. OpenAI and Anthropic are racing each other on technology, while facing the profit pressures of looming public listings. This year, both firms have released new AI models that represent a clear jump from prior versions. (45)","Risks that were once theoretical about AI now seem real. Over the past few months, there have been too many examples of AI agents acting autonomously, and maliciously, for us to ignore the threat.","We are at a moment like the dawn of the nuclear weapons age. So long as AI supremacy is tied to national security in the U.S. and China, there is a strong incentive for policymakers to take a light touch with AI, for fear of a model gap, as John F. Kennedy might have called it.","It took an arms race coupled with the horrifying examples of Hiroshima and Nagasaki to get the U.S. and U.S.S.R. to negotiate arms-control agreements. Now, global governments risk making the same mistake. “There is no day after tomorrow if China wins,” Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said on Tuesday. “If they were to pull away from us on AI, then nothing would matter.”","[A] Implicit in the birth of OpenAI was the idea that AI could lead to very bad outcomes, including the extinction of the human race, and that unregulated commercial pressures would hasten those disasters.","[B] Anthropic’s researchers have proved that AI will certainly kill all humans within a decade.","[C] These models are very good at both cybercrime and cyberdefense and can work on problems for weeks without human intervention. They also exhibit “alignment” issues, meaning they can fail to remain aligned with human intentions and interests.","[D] Governments avoid a light touch with AI because they no longer fear that another country will open up a decisive model gap.","[E] “The U.S. government, and all other governments, should regulate the development of SMI,” Altman wrote in his 2015 essay.","[F] In fact, the quote is more than a century old, from a glowing 1921 New York Times Book Review of Social Decay and Regeneration by R. Austin Freeman. The book argued that industrial automation would be the end of the world as we know it.","[G] Today, the U.S. has 70% more accounting firm employees than it had in 1990, and they now make up a larger portion of the workforce than they did 35 years ago."],"items":[{"number":41,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"F","kicker":"【答案】F","analysis":["【定位】第二段段首；第三段开始总评技术末日论。","【解析】第一段说这句话似乎可能出自2026年 AI 研究者；【F】用 In fact, the quote is more than a century old 形成强转折，并交代它来自1921年书评。后文 headlined “Man Devoured by His Machines”继续描述该书评，第三段随即把话题提升为 Tech doomsaying…hardly new。","逐项分析"]},{"number":42,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"A","kicker":"【答案】A","analysis":["【定位】第五段段末；第六段转向 Anthropic 新警告。","【解析】前文写 Altman 称超人类机器智能是人类存续的最大威胁，并创办 OpenAI；【A】中的 Implicit in the birth of OpenAI 精准回指这一事件，并把担忧落实为 extinction 与 unregulated commercial pressures。第六段 The worries hit a new gear 承接该担忧并推进到 Anthropic。","逐项分析"]},{"number":43,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"E","kicker":"【答案】E","analysis":["【定位】第七段段末；第八段转向历史经验。","【解析】空前说 Altman 和 Amodei 一边获得巨额资金，一边呼吁国际合作监管；【E】直接引用 Altman 的话，要求美国和其他政府监管 SMI development，把前句的 regulating AI 落到具体主张。第八段 As the doomsday scenarios mount 则转向这些警告是否应验的问题。","逐项分析"]},{"number":44,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"G","kicker":"【答案】G","analysis":["【定位】第八段段末；第九段提出“这次可能不同”。","【解析】空前说电子表格软件曾被认为会消灭会计职业；【G】用 Today 和70% more accounting firm employees 完成证据链，证明预言落空。第九段 You should always be suspicious…but this time may be different 借此转入 AI 与既往技术不同的可能性。","逐项分析"]},{"number":45,"stem":"","options":[],"answer":"C","kicker":"【答案】C","analysis":["【定位】第九段段末；第十段确认风险变为现实。","【解析】空前说 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 的新模型明显跃升；【C】中的 These models 回指 new AI models，并说明它们擅长攻防、能数周无人类干预地工作，还会出现 alignment 问题。第十段 Risks that were once theoretical now seem real 随即把这些能力风险确认为现实威胁。","逐项分析","干扰项设置","【B】利用 Anthropic 和 kill all humans 制造恐慌诱饵，但删去了 could 与 >10% 的概率限定；【D】复现 light touch 和 model gap，却把“因怕落后而放松监管”反转成“不再怕而严格监管”。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语新题型大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。目前是在测试阶段，该题型仅提供到12月底。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.23 精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":675926,"date":"2026-09-23","range":"","title":"AI Doomers Can’t Stop Dooming. It’s Time","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.23 精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.23 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":56199,"date":"2026-09-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.23 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.23检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":57828,"date":"2026-09-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.23检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.23检验题__新题型__7选5(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":77043,"date":"2026-09-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.23检验题__新题型__7选5(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"9.23杂志排版(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":730052,"date":"2026-09-23","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.23杂志排版(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
